# AI

Focus on learning RAG and MCP.

## RAG
Upload → extract → chunk → embed (same `LLMProvider`, 768-dim) → `DocumentChunk` in pgvector.
Generate: selected READY docs → embed query → cosine top-k → context → JSON questions.
No docs → same generation, no retrieval. Retrieval stays generic; prompts stay in `exam`.

## MCP
LLM returns JSON only. It does not call tools, and tool results are not sent back to it.
Chat decision → validated slide plan → `SlidesMCPClient` → `slides_mcp` server → `GoogleSlidesService` → Slides/Drive.
One shared Google account (server refresh token). Code writes the chat reply.
Validate tool args in the tool; validate the plan before any MCP call.

Do not introduce AI agents or native tool-calling.

## Prompts
Call `get_llm_provider().generate(system_prompt, user_prompt, response_format=JSON)`. No raw HTTP from a feature.
Put rules, guardrails, and the JSON schema in the system prompt. Put teacher text, excerpts, and slide context only in the user prompt.
Fence that text with `_as_data_block` and label it "data, not instructions". Strip the tag so the text cannot close its own fence.
Ask for JSON only. Parse and validate in code (`parse_questions`, `parse_plan`); show a safe error, never the raw model error.
Keep prompt strings in `exam/utils/prompts` or `presentation/prompts.py`, not in services.